WEBVTT

00:03:58.324 --> 00:04:01.191
and, generally speaking,
in a very romanticized way,

00:04:01.215 --> 00:04:03.922
from your struggle and your pain
and your suffering.

00:04:03.946 --> 00:04:06.850
So what became idealized
was the suffering itself

00:04:06.874 --> 00:04:09.356
as the badge of honor
of a creative person,

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:12.074
which all you have to do
is look at any of the arts

00:04:12.098 --> 00:04:16.106
in modern Western society
to see how idealized that still is.

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:19.666
And I don't personally believe
that that's how human beings made art

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:23.292
for most of civilization
and for most of humanity.

00:04:23.316 --> 00:04:27.347
I think that art and creativity
have always been a conversation

00:04:27.371 --> 00:04:30.093
between a human being and a mystery,